WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.758
Internal network abuse occurs when an application feature that fetches URLs or integrates with remote systems can reach services that the attacker cannot access directly.

2
00:00:09.758 --> 00:00:15.765
Payment environments often contain internal services that should not be reachable from user-controlled input.

3
00:00:15.765 --> 00:00:19.586
Cloud metadata exploitation is a serious SSRF scenario.

4
00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:27.808
If a workload can reach metadata endpoints, attackers may attempt to obtain temporary credentials or environmental information.

5
00:00:27.808 --> 00:00:33.386
Trust boundary violations happen when applications treat user-provided destinations as safe.

6
00:00:33.386 --> 00:00:42.665
URL fetchers, webhook validators, image importers, document converters, and integration testing features all need careful destination controls.

7
00:00:42.665 --> 00:00:52.922
SSRF defenses work best when application validation is paired with network segmentation, egress filtering, and monitoring for unusual server-initiated traffic.

8
00:00:52.922 --> 00:00:56.833
Segment networks and restrict access to internal payment systems.

9
00:00:56.833 --> 00:01:01.203
Validate and restrict outbound URLs using allow lists where possible.

10
00:01:01.203 --> 00:01:06.023
Apply egress filtering and monitor unusual server-initiated requests.

11
00:01:06.023 --> 00:01:09.904
